# Accordion

Accordion groups related sections and lets people reveal only the information they need. It supports single or multiple open items, controlled state, disabled items, and keyboard navigation.

## Default

<DocsExample title="Accordion example" source={accordionExampleSource} htmlSource={accordionExampleHtmlSource}><AccordionExample /></DocsExample>

## Multiple and disabled items

Use `type="multiple"` when sections can be understood independently. Add `disabled` to individual items that are visible but unavailable. Items can also include an optional icon from the Aesir icon registry.

<DocsExample title="Multiple accordion with a disabled item" source={accordionMultipleExampleSource} htmlSource={accordionMultipleExampleHtmlSource}><AccordionMultipleExample /></DocsExample>

## Controlled state

Bind `value` when another control needs to open or close accordion sections.

<DocsExample title="Controlled accordion example" source={accordionControlledExampleSource} htmlSource={accordionControlledExampleHtmlSource}><AccordionControlledExample /></DocsExample>

## Custom content

Use the `itemContent` snippet for richer layouts while keeping the same item state and keyboard behavior.

<DocsExample title="Accordion with custom content" source={accordionCustomContentExampleSource} htmlSource={accordionCustomContentExampleHtmlSource}><AccordionCustomContentExample /></DocsExample>

## With media

Add an `image` or `video` to the same item data to enable the media layout. Opening an item updates the media on the right; no second component or mode prop is needed. Videos autoplay muted with `playsinline` and `loop`. The active item remains open so the media and its explanation never get out of sync.

<DocsExample title="Accordion with changing media example" source={accordionMediaExampleSource} htmlSource={accordionMediaExampleHtmlSource}><AccordionMediaExample /></DocsExample>
